    {
      "kind": "text",
      "tag": "h6",
      "text": "Adaptive Voice Coaching"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "I designed a voice-first coaching layer that delivers real-time, context-aware guidance without adding cognitive load, timed to the exact moment it’s needed: a stop sign, an intersection, a lane change. Voice-frequency studies shaped the interaction model, balancing how often the coach speaks against how much a new driver can actually absorb behind the wheel."
    },
    {
      "kind": "image",
      "src": "https://framerusercontent.com/images/0IfcA7g5ZulWmTwQyunwkSKyu0Y.png",
      "alt": "",
      "name": "Fill Your Image Here"
    },
    {
      "kind": "component",
      "name": "Highlighter Tag",
      "controls": {
        "title": "Scenario Coverage"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "tag": "h6",
      "text": "From Teen Driving to a Coaching System"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "What began as a single concept for coaching teen drivers became a reusable pattern system I built across parking, intersections, stop signs, turns, lane changes, and speed management.\nEach pattern shares the same voice-first coaching logic, so adding a new driving scenario means composing existing building blocks, not starting from scratch. It’s a system, not a one-off feature."
    },
